// The part-2 CONSUMER world — a reducer guest that IMPORTS cadenza:syntax as a content-addressed +hash
// dep and drives a call into it. It reuses the `cadenza:agent-kernel` reducer contract (kv/fold/types,
// vendored in agent-kernel.wit) so the host drives it exactly like any reducer, AND adds the
// cadenza:syntax/parse import (vendored in syntax.wit) that the compose path resolves + links.
//
// THE +HASH IMPORT: `import cadenza:syntax/parse@0.0.0+SYNTAXGUESTHASH` — the FULL content-addressed
// name the kernel registers the dep under (wasm_host.rs compose). `+SYNTAXGUESTHASH` is a PLACEHOLDER
// token v-nix's flake derivation regex-replaces with the resolved packages.syntax-guest content-hash at
// build time (the source stays templated; option-i, v-ah-ruled). @0.0.0 = the producer package version
// (compose's bare_iface_name strips @ver+hash for the export-match, but a declared import needs a ver).
package cadenza:syntax-consumer;

world consumer {
  // The reducer's session KV (direct host import, non-effect — §4b), same as the reducer world.
  import cadenza:agent-kernel/kv;
  // The content-addressed cadenza:syntax dep: the flavor-2 direct linked call target. The +hash is
  // templated at build (placeholder SYNTAXGUESTHASH). Only `parse` is needed for the read-sexpr demo.
  import cadenza:syntax/parse@0.0.0+SYNTAXGUESTHASH;
  // The guest exports the fold entrypoint the host drives per event (same contract as the reducer world).
  export cadenza:agent-kernel/fold;
}
